# qkt portfolio research project

This project was generated by `qkt create template --kind portfolio`.

It is a research scaffold for testing multiple strategies as one book. It does
not configure a live broker.

## First Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
$EDITOR .env
make backtest
```

## Environment Values

Required:

- `QKT_IMAGE_TAG`: QKT image tag. The generated default pins to the QKT version
  that created this project.
- `BACKTEST_FROM`, `BACKTEST_TO`: research window.

Usually tune:

- `QKT_STARTING_BALANCE`: portfolio starting capital and allocation base.

Keep `.env` out of Git.

## Commands

- `make backtest`: run `strategies/portfolio.qkt` across the configured window.
- `make up`: start the QKT daemon for local portfolio exercises.
- `make deploy`: deploy the portfolio book as `BOOK` (`portfolio` by default).
- `make resync-dry-run`: validate a portfolio replacement without changing the running book.
- `make resync`: replace the running portfolio book.
- `make reconcile`: compare QKT ledger to configured account state.
- `make logs`: tail daemon logs.

## Strategy Flow

The generated `portfolio.qkt` references `trend.qkt` and `mean_reversion.qkt`.
Tune the component strategies and risk config together, then rerun `make
backtest` before deploying locally.

Scaffolded by qkt v{{QKT_VERSION}}.
